{
  "_comment": "Font registry for the local FFmpeg fontfile= rendering system. Each key is a font family name (matching the frontend's fontFamily field). Values map weight (as string) to {normal, italic} relative paths under backend/fonts/. Add new families by dropping their .ttf/.otf files under backend/fonts/<FamilyName>/ and extending this JSON.",
  "_comment_weight_coverage": "Genuine upstream typeface limits, not bugs — font_manager's nearest-weight snap ladder is the correct, honest fallback for these, not a gap to silently paper over: Lato ships only {100,300,400,700,900} (no true 500/600 Medium/SemiBold cut exists upstream — Google Fonts has no Lato variable font); Oswald and Space Grotesk are static-only sets topping out at 700 (no 800/900, no italic at all — Space Grotesk's upstream variable font's own wght axis caps at 700); Open Sans tops out at 800 (no 900). Every other family (Inter, Montserrat, Roboto, Poppins) has real files for the full 400/500/600/700/900 set requested + italic.",
